{"title":"2024 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 19","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><dl><dd><i>The following problem is from the <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">2024 AMC 10A #19</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_12\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2024 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 12\">2024 AMC 12A #12</a>, so those problems redirect to this page.</i></dd></dl>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_19\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 19</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Similar_to_previous_solutions)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Similar to previous solutions)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_5_(similar_to_other_solutions)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5 (similar to other solutions)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_grogg007\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by grogg007</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Power_Solve\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Power Solve</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Detailed_Video_Solution_by_Scholars_Foundation\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Detailed Video Solution by Scholars Foundation</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Pi_Academy\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Pi Academy</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_SpreadTheMathLove\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">11</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by SpreadTheMathLove</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-12\"><a href=\"#Video_solution_by_TheNeuralMathAcademy\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">12</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video solution by TheNeuralMathAcademy</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-13\"><a href=\"#Video_solution_by_MaffyTaffy\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">13</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video solution by MaffyTaffy</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-14\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">14</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_19\">Problem 19</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 19\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The first three terms of a geometric sequence are the integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/d/48dbd0f28f101d984ab3588b611c8500d0edd9c3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,\\,720,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"55\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/1/5b1d6265e67657b5886ce257671d45ff9c0282eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"12\" height=\"16\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/1/7d1cd2aba18c770b36f6aeee728175be9de5a155.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a&lt;720&lt;b.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"100\" height=\"15\" /> What is the sum of the digits of the least possible value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/e/49e9ecda4a741b4ea1e4e0bcfc0df342e8551a68.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b?$\" width=\"16\" height=\"12\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/8/3f8594e8db24edda3363beb4be644084a6187bcf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) } 9 \\qquad \\textbf{(B) } 12 \\qquad \\textbf{(C) } 16 \\qquad \\textbf{(D) } 18 \\qquad \\textbf{(E) } 21$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"392\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For a geometric sequence, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/c/bbc25360d49891f1f0be19a847c887a51421a8c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ab=720^2=2^8 3^4 5^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"152\" height=\"17\" />, and we can test values for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />. We find that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/e/2de196c4f91357fa8cb50e78ef0246c3c4251cdf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b=768$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"61\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/d/b1d697e139473e02accba9cf5eba48254ee5d3c2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=675$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"63\" height=\"14\" /> works, and we can test multiples of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> in between the two values. Finding that none of the multiples of 5 divide <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/4/724f96d53f9d528a8c366c309f538525d4c89ff9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$720^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"37\" height=\"17\" /> besides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/9/2d90a8212646e076fae82808b7469d47c369a370.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$720$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" /> itself, we know that the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/f/b0fcffabb20ca7d63418a0a05c8b0747ae8dffff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7+6+8=\\boxed{\\textbf{(E) } 21}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"161\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>(Note: To find the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> without bashing, we can observe that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/e/a5efb3bc415def343ddc4f461d5d608c5dd6c548.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^8=256$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"70\" height=\"17\" />, and that multiplying it by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> gives us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/c/7dcd87737949216c3dbdabe299c062da63660425.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$768$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" />, which is really close to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/9/2d90a8212646e076fae82808b7469d47c369a370.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$720$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" />. ~ YTH)\n</p><p>Note: The reason why <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/d/c9d20cfd550439ed3245ff9a1694e1c867046fbb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ab=720^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"78\" height=\"17\" /> is because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/6/fb65000e2227715abc37640055d26ca157b3c4b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b/720 = 720/a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"116\" height=\"20\" />. Rearranging this gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/7/5f7438f101cf8e7cc834e0ab2e6dba80beb1ac84.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ab = 720^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"78\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p>~eevee9406\n</p><p>Note: Another reason that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/d/c9d20cfd550439ed3245ff9a1694e1c867046fbb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ab=720^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"78\" height=\"17\" /> is because the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/6/fd62b7f07c4a7fb5f89504017bf38bd18f481363.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{ab}=720$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"86\" height=\"21\" /> (as the middle term in a geometric series is always the geometric mean [the geometric mean is the square root of the product of the first and last terms of the series]) and squaring on both sides results in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/d/c9d20cfd550439ed3245ff9a1694e1c867046fbb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ab=720^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"78\" height=\"17\" />.\n</p><p>~ThatPrimePunnyGuy\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/e/10e09d95b64559afdf6643819105dbe8ab77a13b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$720 = 2^4 \\cdot 3^2 \\cdot 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"122\" height=\"17\" />. We want to find factors <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/b/d5b7ad4c34a3f2485fb4fd2342d49e605df553fc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y&gt;x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"44\" height=\"13\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/7/c471843498de1d9d0b05ad7f32eab45e216577b4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{y}{x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"12\" height=\"33\" />, the ratio, is minimized. To do this, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> should be as large as possible, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> should be just slightly larger than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />. Additionally, to ensure <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> are both integers, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> should both be a factor of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/9/2d90a8212646e076fae82808b7469d47c369a370.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$720$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p><p>After experimenting, we see this is achieved when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/7/bf709e521fe3f0bae584d735bda8a7c0b5627984.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"51\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/5/e45a63c78330a7020ad39fd035c818528f54ff46.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=15$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"52\" height=\"13\" />, which means our value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/5/9858472e35d5c697b1a7e79c3a851c92bdd1edcd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$720 \\cdot \\frac{16}{15} = 768$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"116\" height=\"38\" />. Therefore, the sum is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/f/b0fcffabb20ca7d63418a0a05c8b0747ae8dffff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7+6+8=\\boxed{\\textbf{(E) } 21}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"161\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~i_am_suk_at_math_2\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Similar_to_previous_solutions.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Similar_to_previous_solutions)\">Solution 3 (Similar to previous solutions)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Similar to previous solutions)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>To minimize the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />, where it has to be an integer, and it has to be greater than 720, we can express the common ratio as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/f/bff900ab88b7b07f19773c8b995ea72672f620d8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{n+1}{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"48\" height=\"38\" />, where the value has to be greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/3/0e3efd9b14723a92c2ae891fe27780d5f8e2b215.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" /> have to be factors of 720. Since the bigger the denominator gets, the smaller the value of the fraction, we essentially have to find the biggest value for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, where itself and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/3/0e3efd9b14723a92c2ae891fe27780d5f8e2b215.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" /> are factors of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/9/2d90a8212646e076fae82808b7469d47c369a370.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$720$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" />. From here, we can check whether <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/f/c6f2910014e4080fe5ae593d5a94413d03480953.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n(n+1) = 720$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"121\" height=\"20\" /> yields an integer root, which it doesn't. So, then we check the next biggest factor of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/9/2d90a8212646e076fae82808b7469d47c369a370.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$720$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" />, which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/2/c62a47cbc153efdf4611d8660429ea879be3f192.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$360$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/1/861d80edb0e7aecf85155cd9e821f2ddf5036602.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n(n+1) = 360$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"121\" height=\"20\" />, this doesn't have an integer root either. So, then we check the next biggest factor which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/d/efd7f90b1c0d050ea71e884260078e17d6ffadfd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$240$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/0/f30c1b48ad47eb2fad88f0ba6e52a79fc7203606.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n(n+1) = 240$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"121\" height=\"20\" />, which we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/9/f1965fae079a9ba2c0726c307070c2355dfcb213.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> as a root. This means the common ration is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/4/a949780723f1a2d2607527211acad61cfb27a513.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{16}{15}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"24\" height=\"38\" />. We then multiply <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/4/a949780723f1a2d2607527211acad61cfb27a513.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{16}{15}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"24\" height=\"38\" /> times <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/9/2d90a8212646e076fae82808b7469d47c369a370.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$720$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" /> and add up the digits getting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/8/29861c9f09ef185382d1986c2a2c8838596b7c1a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(E) } 21}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"65\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~yuvag\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let the common ratio of the geometric sequence be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/2/e32f96b310bbe6cd6981b6c1da83fe7905ea3116.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{x}{y}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"12\" height=\"36\" />, with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/1/7b18737adf5e499e3c33b3c5516930d328ce5a13.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x&gt;y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"43\" height=\"13\" />. This means that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/d/6ed3704f275660a8d89e053b142753a0467f8919.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$720(\\frac{x}{y})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"58\" height=\"38\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/8/968d4de147383fb7efe794f953c411784e29824a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$720(\\frac{y}{x})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"58\" height=\"34\" /> must both be integers, therefore <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> are both factors of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/9/2d90a8212646e076fae82808b7469d47c369a370.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$720$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" />. We would achieve the smallest ratio <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/2/e32f96b310bbe6cd6981b6c1da83fe7905ea3116.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{x}{y}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"12\" height=\"36\" /> if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> are consecutive, so by listing out the factors of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/9/2d90a8212646e076fae82808b7469d47c369a370.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$720$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" />, we find that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/9/f1965fae079a9ba2c0726c307070c2355dfcb213.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/5/9a5b4928c8fe50ce3c2428da3bee3505e891b788.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> are the only consecutive factors (any factors larger than these would result in the ratio simplifying, making it larger than just using consecutive integers). <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/9/f1965fae079a9ba2c0726c307070c2355dfcb213.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/5/9a5b4928c8fe50ce3c2428da3bee3505e891b788.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> are the largest, so we find the common ratio to be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/3/ca368c7e4361f802c5179eb61e63bc4e903954a2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{16}{15}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"24\" height=\"38\" />, making <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/4/e14a08a18d49342b038ec462108e3b23246afeff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b=720(\\frac{16}{15})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"97\" height=\"38\" /> giving us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/c/7dcd87737949216c3dbdabe299c062da63660425.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$768$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" />. The sum of its digits is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/8/29861c9f09ef185382d1986c2a2c8838596b7c1a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(E) } 21}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"65\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~lisztepos\n</p><p>~ small edit by RoyalPawn38\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_5_.28similar_to_other_solutions.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5_(similar_to_other_solutions)\">Solution 5 (similar to other solutions)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5 (similar to other solutions)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We look for the smallest possible increasing ratio in the geometric sequence for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/9/2d90a8212646e076fae82808b7469d47c369a370.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$720$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />.\nFirst, we find the prime factorization of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/9/2d90a8212646e076fae82808b7469d47c369a370.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$720$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" />, which is really easy <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/7/5e7afa3d7337d9b9c0825787382dcc9e8f16df3e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$720=2^4\\cdot3^2\\cdot5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"122\" height=\"17\" />. Then, we look for the closest possible fraction-ratio out of the primes, and after a quick look, it's easy to see it is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/5/9a5b4928c8fe50ce3c2428da3bee3505e891b788.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/9/f1965fae079a9ba2c0726c307070c2355dfcb213.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. Now that we found our ratio, we multiply <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/9/2d90a8212646e076fae82808b7469d47c369a370.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$720$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" /> by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/3/ca368c7e4361f802c5179eb61e63bc4e903954a2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{16}{15}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"24\" height=\"38\" /> to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/c/7dcd87737949216c3dbdabe299c062da63660425.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$768$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" />, so the sum of the digits of the least possible value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/8/29861c9f09ef185382d1986c2a2c8838596b7c1a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(E) } 21}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"65\" height=\"30\" />..\n</p><p>~hashbrown2009\n~GoldemGem4848 did the latex\n</p><p>NOTE: It's not 9/8 because we want it to be as close as possible to 1 ~gabrielle.esther\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_grogg007\">Video Solution by <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php/User:grogg007\">grogg007</a></span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by grogg007\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=-VWz8lEBv0I\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=-VWz8lEBv0I</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Power_Solve\">Video Solution by Power Solve</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Power Solve\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=B0JOMiiCtAo\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=B0JOMiiCtAo</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Detailed_Video_Solution_by_Scholars_Foundation\">Detailed Video Solution by Scholars Foundation</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Detailed Video Solution by Scholars Foundation\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=JoF4-fo7W1w&amp;pp=ygULYW1jIDEwIDIwMjQ%3D\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=JoF4-fo7W1w&amp;pp=ygULYW1jIDEwIDIwMjQ%3D</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Pi_Academy\">Video Solution by Pi Academy</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Pi Academy\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/fW7OGWee31c?si=oq7toGPh2QaksLHE\">https://youtu.be/fW7OGWee31c?si=oq7toGPh2QaksLHE</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_SpreadTheMathLove\">Video Solution by SpreadTheMathLove</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by SpreadTheMathLove\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/otByKTvfE7I?si=3x83heqecMIKYCMD\">https://youtu.be/otByKTvfE7I?si=3x83heqecMIKYCMD</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_solution_by_TheNeuralMathAcademy\">Video solution by TheNeuralMathAcademy</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=12\" title=\"Edit section: Video solution by TheNeuralMathAcademy\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4b_YLnyegtw&amp;t=4056s\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4b_YLnyegtw&amp;t=4056s</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_solution_by_MaffyTaffy\">Video solution by MaffyTaffy</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=13\" title=\"Edit section: Video solution by MaffyTaffy\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://